### Draft caption content for discussion

**Figure 1, if paired.** Transfer-network context and Premier League entry by age in recorded seasons 2012/13–2024/25. (a) The whole-network backbone retains 383 clubs and 1,396 directed routes carrying 5,271 of 16,636 eligible transfer records (31.7%). A route is retained when its directed disparity score is strictly below alpha = 0.20 at either eligible endpoint. Colours and symbols identify the five saved Louvain communities; arrows run from origin to destination and shaft width represents transfer count. Node sizes increase with the square root of each club's original incoming plus outgoing transfer count and stay fixed across cutoffs. The graph pools ages and includes Premier League and other destinations. (b) Histogram of 999 age-label shuffles within origin club and recorded season. The statistic is the joining rate for ages 30+ minus that for under 30, in percentage points. The observed gap is -2.42 points (12.14% versus 14.56%), compared with a shuffled mean of -1.31 points; the empirical one-sided p-value is 0.098. The legend's +/-0.83 is one standard deviation of shuffled gaps, and the fitted normal curve is illustrative. The lower observed rate provides limited evidence against this conditional null.

**Figure 2, if both panels selected.** Guardian tone and coverage around selected Premier League signings. (a) Mean RoBERTa tone before and after signing for 67 signings aged 30+ and 753 under 30. Each signing contributes one period mean, using days -365 to -8 and +8 to +365, excluding liveblogs and match reports and requiring at least five scored sentences in each period. Scores are P(positive) minus P(negative). Older-group means are 0.0914 before and 0.0838 after; younger-group means are 0.1253 and 0.1117. The older-minus-younger difference in signing-level changes is +0.0060 score units (two-sided p = 0.7558 from 5,000 age-label shuffles within season). Markers are descriptive group means; no uncertainty intervals are shown. The comparison gives no clear evidence of different tone changes, with limited sensitivity to smaller differences. (b) Median distinct article counts per signing in the same time windows, using all article types and all 1,332 selected signings, including zero coverage (88 older, 1,244 younger). Medians are 27.5 versus 12 before and 47.5 versus 35 after. The two panels have different eligibility rules and denominators.

**Table 1.** Agreement of four sentiment instruments with 196 hand-labelled sentences after excluding four wrong-person cases. Rho is Spearman rank correlation with the ordered human labels; 95% intervals are percentile intervals from 2,000 sentence bootstrap resamples. Sign agreement uses the 85 positive or negative labels. Three-class accuracy uses a neutral band of +/-0.05 for RoBERTa and VADER and exactly zero for both Bing variants. Only 14 evaluable cases concern older players, leaving age-specific validity uncertain. Use the approved rounded cells unchanged.

### Saved-artifact review and provenance limits

- The selected H1 PDF is 3.58 by 3.40 inches, with embedded Arial at 9–9.5 pt. Its axes and histogram are readable in the inspected render; its legend needs the SD explanation above. The observed statistic is a gap, so its orange mark is not an age-group series.
- The saved backbone comparison is 7.16 by 2.82 inches with three cutoffs. Its tiny routes and arrowheads limit detailed reading in each small tile. A single alpha 0.20 panel would give structural context more space, but individual club labels are absent. A paired export has not been produced or verified. Community names identify the saved groups, not exclusive membership in a named club's league. Whole-network R parity agrees at 0.20; the separate 29/30 overall tie and unverified live browser QA remain in provenance.
- The supplied PNAS template recommends 17.8 cm for a full-width figure and defines a 512 TeX-point text width with 247-point columns. Existing 7.16-inch exports need sizing to that template. Proposed dimensions are planning estimates, not a compiled fit test. Maintain at least 8 pt legends and about 9 pt ticks at final size; reallocate explicitly if captions and labels do not fit. No approved passage is silently compressed.
- The two existing Guardian PDFs are [adjusted monthly arcs](../../paper/figures/fig_h2b_arc_paper.pdf), 7.16 by 4.60 inches, and [tone-level gaps plus modelled coverage ratios](../../paper/figures/fig_h2b_tone_coverage.pdf), 7.16 by 3.10 inches. Both are H2b-specific presentations, not selected core H2 displays. They use embedded Arial at 8–10 pt. The gap/coverage PDF's smallest labels are crowded, and its coverage axis needs the log(1 + count) interpretation if reused. Their displayed ranges trace to estimate +/-1.96 shuffle SD, exponentiated for coverage; do not call these conventional confidence intervals. The adjusted arcs have no shaded bands.
- `pnas_report/output/guardian_text_findings/` is still absent. The plotting producer would also overwrite the two earlier-draft compatibility PDFs, so any approved production needs isolated destinations and a fresh-context agent as already required.
- Read-only file comparison found byte identity for all six copied tables with same-named originals: coverage, H2b arc, H2b controls, validation metrics, confusion counts and signing tone. The copied raw arc has 192 rows across four models, whereas original `a1_age30_arc.csv` has 96 rows for RoBERTa and VADER. All 96 common rows match after renaming `method` to `model` and normalising numeric formatting. The other two instruments lack a matching original monthly export in that directory. Do not describe the entire four-model copy as independently matched.
- Raw monthly arcs first average each signing within a month, then average available signings and apply a three-month rolling mean separately on either side of signing. Monthly membership varies. Their saved bands bootstrap signings separately in each month, then smooth the interval endpoints; they are not intervals for the between-age difference in period changes. If an arc is preferred, use a single RoBERTa panel, explain those distinctions and discuss bands explicitly. The recommended period-mean presentation avoids that mismatch. Omit the historical unverified H2 between-age interval.
- No external literature claim, new statistical analysis or additional robustness check was introduced. The approved sample description, H1 sensitivity passage, feeder role and six-page allocation are preserved.

