- H1 joining rates: 129/1,063 = 12.14% for 30+, 2,267/15,573 = 14.56% for under 30. Older-minus-younger gap -2.42 percentage points; 999 age-label shuffles within origin club and recorded season; mean shuffled gap -1.31, sample SD 0.83; empirical lower-tail one-sided p = 0.098. The normal curve is illustrative, and +/-0.83 is one shuffle SD, not a confidence interval. Lower observed older-group rate with limited evidence against the conditional null; no causal or equal-rate conclusion. Full approved fixed-player sensitivity remains Results prose.
- Figure 2's separate Guardian sample has 820 sufficiently covered signings (67 older, 753 younger). Before days -365 to -8, after +8 to +365; exclude liveblogs/match reports, require five scored sentences each period. Monthly curves average signing-months and use saved three-month smoothing separately on each side. Monthly membership varies. Dots show means of signing-period means with equal signing weight, NOT averages of the smoothed curve. Dot centres at -6/+6 are display positions; short horizontal segments are fixed symbols, NOT intervals or durations. H2 compares signing-level changes: main RoBERTa gap +0.0060 score units, season-restricted permutation p = 0.7558; no clear age difference, with limited sensitivity to smaller differences. Do not use the unverified historical H2 between-age interval.
- Keep the four-instrument validation table: data/dataset_nlp/results/b9_model_scores.csv, subset "all scored". 196 evaluable human labels after four wrong-person exclusions; sign agreement denominator 85; Spearman intervals from 2,000 sentence bootstrap resamples. Only 14 older-player cases, so age-specific validity remains uncertain. Approved rounded cells/note are in evidence_and_sources.md. It is a table with its own space allocation, not a figure slot.

